{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013th7s6Mx5nafpuYCno23PY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The `ogx` collection has a direct requirement for `pymilvus>=2.4.10` for various architectures. But the `rhai` collection doesn't have pymilvus directly - it's a transitive dependency through `langchain-milvus`.\n\nThe key insight here is:\n- `langchain-milvus 0.4.0` requires `pymilvus<4.0,>=3.0.0`\n- This means `langchain-milvus 0.4.0` requires pymilvus 3.x, but NOT 2.x\n- The `ogx` collection pins pymilvus to `>=2.4.10` which is a 2.x version\n- Since `rhai` has `langchain-milvus` as a top-level requirement with no version constraint, it resolved to 0.4.0, which then demands pymilvus 3.x\n- But `pymilvus 3.x` was just released a couple days ago, creating this conflict with the older 2.x requirement from `ogx`\n- On x86_64, all available pymilvus 3.x versions fall within Fromager's 3-day cooldown window, so they can't be used\n- On aarch64, there's no source distribution available for pymilvus 3.x at all, which blocks the build entirely\n- I should verify whether `langchain-milvus 0.4.0` itself is a recent release that might have introduced this pymilvus 3.x requirement\n\n, and check if there are any version pins elsewhere in the dependency tree","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_read_input_tokens":71925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":400,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":12},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77a3f021-627e-47e4-9986-5fd96a09bf56","uuid":"2f8ee0cc-29fe-4a52-a8d8-6fc175cdbafe","timestamp":"2026-07-20T22:08:09.850Z","request_id":"req_vrtx_011CdE56iHHCgXrdRde8oeyx"}
